[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Ruy Lopez: Closed"]
[ECO "C84"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "queenside-space,central-pawns"]
[Kind "main"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 { Attacks the knight that defends e5. The threat is slow, so Black has time to ask the bishop a question. } 3... a6 { Asks the bishop to decide. If it takes on c6, Black gets two bishops; if it retreats, ...b5 gains space. }
4. Ba4
( 4. Bxc6 dxc6 { The recapture opens the bishop on c8 and gives Black two bishops. } 5. O-O ( 5. d3 f6 6. Nbd2 c5 ) 5... f6 { Defends e5 with a pawn and keeps the bishops free. } 6. d4 exd4 7. Nxd4 c5 { Hits the knight, and after it moves Black trades queens and keeps the bishop pair. } 8. Nb3 Qxd1 9. Rxd1 Bg4 )
4... Nf6 { Develops and attacks e4, so White must decide how to defend it. }
5. O-O
( 5. d3 d6 { Gives e5 a pawn defender and frees the c8 bishop. } 6. c3 Be7 7. O-O O-O )
5... Be7 { Develops the bishop and prepares to castle. }
6. Re1 6... b5 { Gains space and asks the bishop to leave the long diagonal. If it takes on c6, Black recaptures. }
7. Bb3 7... d6 { Gives e5 a pawn defender and frees the c8 bishop. }
8. c3 8... O-O { Castle: the king is safe and the rook can join the centre. }
9. h3 9... Nb8 { The knight on c6 does little, so it heads back via b8 to d7, where it supports e5 and the centre. }
10. d4 10... Nbd7 11. Nbd2 11... Bb7 { Puts the last minor piece on the long diagonal, aimed at e4. }
12. Bc2 12... Re8 { Backs up the e5 pawn. Plan: ...Bf8 and ...c5 or ...exd4 to break open the centre. If White plays d5, keep the position closed with ...c6. } *
